+### Refunds 
+
+Sunbit requires that you submit a refund within 180 days from the original payment using the [Dashboard](https://dashboard.stripe.com/payments) or [Refunds API](https://docs.stripe.com/api/refunds/create.md). This is the maximum the payment method allows. Your return policy determines what you offer customers.
+
+Refunds for Sunbit payments are asynchronous and take up to 5 minutes to complete. You can’t cancel Sunbit refunds.
+
+#### Refund process 
+
+Sunbit refunds are never processed as reversals. When you issue a refund, Sunbit cancels any remaining scheduled payments and returns any amounts the customer has already paid. The customer sees the update reflected in their Sunbit account.
+
+#### Tracking refunds 
+
+To check a refund’s status, open the payment in the [Dashboard](https://dashboard.stripe.com/payments) and click **View details** on the refund entry. You can also [retrieve the Refund object](https://docs.stripe.com/api/refunds/retrieve.md) and check its `status` field.
+
