+You can submit evidence and manage Sunbit disputes in the [Dashboard](https://dashboard.stripe.com/disputes) or programmatically using the [Disputes API](https://docs.stripe.com/api/disputes/update.md). In the Dashboard, go to the **Needs response** tab, click the disputed payment, then click **Counter dispute** to submit your evidence, or **Accept dispute** to accept the loss. To submit evidence through the API, upload supporting files using the [Files API](https://docs.stripe.com/api/files/create.md) and include the returned file IDs when you update the [Dispute Evidence object](https://docs.stripe.com/api/disputes/update.md).
+
+#### Dispute outcomes 
+
+If Sunbit resolves the dispute in your favor, Stripe returns the disputed amount to your Stripe balance.
+
+If they rule in favor of the customer, the balance charge becomes permanent.
+
+#### Fees and appeals 
+
+Sunbit doesn’t charge dispute fees. If Sunbit resolves the dispute in your favor, Stripe returns the full disputed amount to your Stripe balance with no fees deducted.
+
+Sunbit dispute decisions are final. You can’t appeal a dispute after Sunbit issues its decision.
+
+#### Fraud and liability 
+
+Customers must authenticate Sunbit payments by logging into their Sunbit account. This requirement helps reduce the risk of fraud or unrecognized payments. While Sunbit covers losses incurred from customer fraud, Stripe might contact you on behalf of Sunbit and request to stop or pause shipment before any losses are incurred. Comply promptly with these requests.
